<article class="env-lemma" id="03AN">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03AN">Lemma <span data-tag="03AN">21.8.2</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a site. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be an abelian presheaf on $\mathcal{C}$. The following are equivalent </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$\mathcal{F}$ is an abelian sheaf on $\mathcal{C}$ and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for every covering $\mathcal{U} = \{ U_ i \to U\} _{i \in I}$ of the site $\mathcal{C}$ the natural map 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \mathcal{F}(U) \to \check{H}^0(\mathcal{U}, \mathcal{F})  \]
</div>
<p>
 (see Sites, Section <a href="/tag/00W1" data-tag="00W1">7.10</a>) is bijective. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is true since the sheaf condition is exactly that $\mathcal{F}(U) \to \check{H}^0(\mathcal{U}, \mathcal{F})$ is bijective for every covering of $\mathcal{C}$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>